<title>NEW ZEALAND: Singapore banks shed Brierley stakes.</title>
<headline>Singapore banks shed Brierley stakes.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand Stock Exchange said on Monday that two Singaporean banks had each shed a 20 percent stake in Brierley Investments Ltd.</p>
<p>The United Overseas Bank Ltd of Singapore and the Overseas-Chinese Banking Corporation Ltd of Singapore both ceased on June 25 to be substantial security holders in Brierley. Both dropped their stake in the company to zero from 20 percent.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4) 473 4746</p>
